class:: HenonC
summary:: Henon map chaotic generator
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic
related:: Classes/HenonN, Classes/HenonL

description::
A cubic-interpolating sound generator based on the difference equation:

teletype::
	x(n+2) = 1 - a * x(n+1)^2 + b * x(n)
::

This equation was discovered by French astronomer Michel Hénon while studying the orbits of stars in globular clusters.

for more information on chaos theory henon formulas:

"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaos_theory"

"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hénon_map"

sclang code translation:

code::
(
var a = 1.4, b = 0.3, x0 = 0, x1 = 1, size = 64;
plot(size.collect { var aux = 1 - (a * (x1 ** 2)) + (b * x0); x0 = x1; x1 = aux; aux });
)
::

classmethods::
method:: ar
argument:: freq
Iteration frequency in Hertz
argument:: a
Equation variable
argument:: b
Equation variable
argument:: x0
Initial value of x
argument:: x1
Second value of x

examples::
code::
(
{
    // Frequency controlled by mouse X (from 20 Hz to the sample rate)
    var freq = MouseX.kr(20, SampleRate.ir);

    // Chaotic signal
    var sig = HenonC.ar(freq);

    // Stereo output with slight attenuation
    (sig * 0.2).dup
}.scope(s);
)

// mouse-control of params
(
{
    var freq = SampleRate.ir / 4;

    // 'a' and 'b' parameters modulated by mouse position
    var a = MouseX.kr(1.0, 1.4);   // Horizontal control
    var b = MouseY.kr(1.0, 0.3);   // Vertical control

    var sig = HenonC.ar(freq, a, b);

    (sig * 0.2).dup
}.scope(s);
)

// randomly modulate params
(
{
    var freq = SampleRate.ir / 8;

    // LFNoise2 modulates 'a' and 'b' with smooth random motion
    var a = LFNoise2.kr(1).range(1.0, 1.4);     // Smooth variation for 'a'
    var b = LFNoise2.kr(1).range(0.15, 0.3);    // Smooth variation for 'b'

    var sig = HenonC.ar(freq, a, b);

    (sig * 0.02).dup
}.scope(s);
)

// as a frequency control
(
{
    // HenonC: a chaotic signal generator
    var chaos = HenonC.ar(
        freq: 40,
        a: MouseX.kr(1.0, 1.4),  // X-axis controls 'a' parameter (horizontal movement)
        b: MouseY.kr(1.0, 0.3)   // Y-axis controls 'b' parameter (vertical movement)
    );

    // Use HenonC output to modulate a sine wave frequency
    var freq = chaos * 800 + 900;

    // Generate stereo audio with a sine oscillator
    SinOsc.ar(freq, 0, 0.04).dup  // 'dup' is shorthand for !2
}.scope(s);
)
::
